[
  {
    "language_code": "",
    "language_probability": 1,
    "text": "Governments are fighting back. America and Europe have blacklisted hundreds of companies in China, Hong, Kong, Turkey, the Emirates and Central Asia. Banks in China and Turkey have grown more nervous about handling Russian payments. Every chip carries tiny printed codes showing who made it and when. Investigators collect them from wreckage, and Ukraine publishes a database of foreign parts found in Russian weapons, so chipmakers can trace where their products ended up. And for Russia, the costs are real. Every chip arrives later, costs more, and might be a fake. But the flow hasn't stopped. It has only become more expensive.",
